{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00052","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00052@rel:R25-11#caeeeace","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00052","release":"R25-11","content":"function OpenKeyValueStorage [SWS_PER_00052] Upstream: RS_PER_00003 , RS_PER_00010 , RS_AP_00119 , RS_AP_00120 , RS_ AP_00121, RS_AP_00127 , RS_AP_00128 , RS_AP_00129 , RS_AP_00135 , RS_AP_00137 , RS_AP_00139 , RS_AP_00144 , RS_AP_00147 , RS_AP_00159 ara::core::Result &lt; SharedHandle &lt; KeyValueStorage &gt; &gt; OpenKeyValue Storage (const ara::core::InstanceSpecifier &amp;kvs) noexcept; Opens a Key-Value Storage. OpenKeyValueStorage will fail with kResourceBusy when the Key-Value Storage is currently being modified by a call from another thread to UpdatePersistency, CleanUpPersistency, Reset Persistency, RecoverKeyValueStorage, or ResetKeyValueStorage. Because multiple threads can access the same Key-Value Storage concurrently, the Key-Value Storage might not be closed when the SharedHandle returned by this function goes out of scope. It will only be closed when all SharedHandles that refer to the same Key-Value Storage went out of scope. Header-Datei #include \"ara/per/key_value_storage.h\" class mono Scope namespace ara::per class mono Exception-Sicherheit exception safe class mono Thread-Sicherheit thread-safe PerErrc ::kStorageNot rollback_semantics class mono Parameter (in) th Parameter th Beschreibung td kvs td The shortName path of a PortPrototype typed by a PersistencyKey ValueStorageInterface. Rückgabewert th Typ th Beschreibung td ara::core::Result &lt; SharedHandle &lt; KeyValueStorage &gt; &gt; td A Result containing a SharedHandle for the KeyValueStorage. In case of an error, it contains any of the errors defined below, or a vendor specific error. Fehler th Fehlercode th Beschreibung td Found td Returned if the passed InstanceSpecifier does not match any PersistencyKeyValueStorageInterface configured for this Executable. td PerErrc ::kPhysicalStorageFailure td no_rollback_semantics Returned if access to the physical storage fails. td PerErrc ::kIntegrityCorrupted td rollback_semantics Returned if stored data cannot be read because the structural integrity is corrupted. td PerErrc ::kValidationFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if the validity of stored data cannot be ensured. td PerErrc ::kEncryptionFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if the decryption of stored data fails. td PerErrc ::kResourceBusy td rollback_semantics Returned if CleanUpPersistency, or ResetPersistency is currently being executed, or if RecoverKeyValueStorage or ResetKeyValue Storage is currently being executed for the same Key-Value Storage. Also, while UpdatePersistency is currently being executed, this error is returned when OpenKeyValueStorage is called outside of the callback registered via RegisterApplicationDataUpdate Callback, or if the used InstanceSpecifier differs from the one provided by the callback. td PerErrc ::kOutOfStorageSpace td no_rollback_semantics Returned if the available physical storage space is insufficient for the values that are added/updated during an implicit update of the Key-Value Storage. td PerErrc ::kQuotaExceeded td rollback_semantics Returned if the values that are added/updated during an implicit update of the Key-Value Storage would exceed the configured maximumAllowedSize. td PerErrc ::kAuthenticationFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if checking the MAC of stored data fails.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"baseline_sync"},"recorded_at":"2026-09-30T16:43:34+00:00","text_key":"52ae048346d1"}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00052","is_dropped":false,"first_active_release":"R25-11","last_active_release":"R25-11","dropped_in":[],"first_dropped_release":null,"absent_before":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11"],"platform_releases":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"latest_platform_release":"R25-11"},"element":{"kind"